Janis Papanagnou wrote:
>
> I wonder how many turns or resp. hits the High Priest at Moloch's Sanctum
> will get, or what else happened here; was I somehow paralysed, maybe?

High priests have a base speed of 15.  You show not Burdened so you have
a base speed of 12 and speed boots to move it up to 15.  A high priest
gets 4 attacks per move and that's reflected in the order - Swing, kick,
cast, cast.

Unless one of those casts slows you down you should get a swing after
every sequence of swing/kick/cast/cast.  I've seen several times when a
high priest gets in a lot of attacks before I can respond.  It's why I
like to be over-prepared and have an insta-kill or extremely high damage
option available for the extremely strong monster encounters.

I think the applicable quote is this one -

"Note that if a monster has two disease, pestilence or famine attacks,
no more than one will be effective in a given turn; if the first is
successful, the second is converted to a stun attack instead."

> You hit the high priestess of Moloch!
...
> The high priestess of Moloch swings her mace.
> The high priestess of Moloch hits!
> The high priestess of Moloch kicks!
> The high priestess of Moloch casts a spell at you!
> Your body is covered with painful wounds!

I think that was the disease hit.

> The high priestess of Moloch points at you, then curses.

I think that was the stun hit.  And the movement cycle starts again
without a move by you ...

